      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "ANTJE CAD → LIFESTYLE  —  Qwen-Image-Edit-2511 (image-to-image)\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. In the LoadImage node (top-left) open the dropdown and pick a CAD\n   drawing. Eight are preloaded: festival_fuchsia_bikini_cad.jpg,\n   neptune_green_bikini_cad.jpg, floralmesh.png, stripedgem.png,\n   redonepiecee.png, valentina.jpg, red.png, ches.png. Or drag your own.\n2. Edit the positive prompt if you like. Suggested:\n   \"Transform this bikini design drawing into a photorealistic lifestyle\n    photograph of a model wearing this exact design, tropical beach golden\n    hour, editorial fashion photography.\"\n3. Press Run. Output lands in output/swimwear/antje_*.png.\n\nMODELS (already installed under models/)\n  diffusion_models/qwen-image-edit-2511.safetensors   (UNETLoader)\n  text_encoders/qwen2.5-vl-7b.safetensors             (CLIPLoader, type qwen_image)\n  vae/qwen-image-vae.safetensors                      (VAELoader)\n\nSAMPLING\n  steps 30, cfg 2.5, euler / simple, denoise 1.0 (Qwen-Image-Edit\n  defaults). The reference drawing is carried into the conditioning by\n  the TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus node (image1 + vae), so the edit stays\n  faithful to the design. The Plus node accepts up to three reference\n  images (image2/image3) if you want to combine views.\n  Negative prompt is intentionally empty; cfg 2.5 is the effective guidance."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
